==English==
{{wikipedia|borscht}}
[[Image:Borscht.jpg|thumb|borscht]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|borsch}}, {{l|en|borshch}}, {{l|en|borsht}}, {{l|en|borschtsch}}

===Etymology===
1884 or 1808. Borrowed from {{bor|en|yi|באָרשט}}, from {{der|en|ru|-}} or {{der|en|uk|борщ}}. {{doublet|en|barszcz}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/bɔːʃt/}}
* {{IPA|en|/bɔɹʃt/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-borscht.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɔː(r)ʃt}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A [[beetroot]] [[soup]] that can be [[serve]]d hot or cold, usually with [[sour cream]].
# Any similar sour soup made of other ingredients such as [[sorrel]], [[cabbage]], [[hogweed]]

